menu "Agent Link StopWatch display"

    config AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_DIRECT_DMA
        bool "Push LVGL bands straight to the CO5300 by DMA (no PSRAM framebuffer)"
        default y
        help
            Each LVGL band is byte-swapped in place and sent to the panel with one asynchronous
            QSPI DMA transfer, so LVGL renders the next band while the previous one is on the wire.
            Off: the old path, which copies every band into a full-screen PSRAM framebuffer
            (M5GFX Panel_fb) and then pushes it to the panel line by line, synchronously.

    config AGENTLINK_DISPLAY_STATS
        bool "Log flush timing every 5 s"
        default n
        help
            Logs flushes, pixels, CPU time spent in the flush callback and time spent waiting
            for the previous DMA transfer (ESP_LOGI, tag sw-display).

endmenu
